{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014ZAZk1BxSqcQa8sN2My6ck","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Suffix-driven GM spelling for metadata-forensics fields (the naming LAWS of lib/knowledge.py, in one place).\n\nAn extractor returns a TYPED raw value; `spell(fmt, field, raw, q)` renders it the way the GM confirmed for that kind of\nfield, keyed on the field name's SUFFIX (never on the day):\n\n  *_uNN_hex        0x + lowercase hex zero-padded to NN/4 digits        (D9  pe.coff_machine_u16_hex \"0x014c\")\n  *_rva_hex        0x + 8 digits (u32 struct width)                    (D10 \"0x00065bd0\"; \"0x65bd0\" REJECTED)\n  *_hex            0x + the struct width the extractor gives via Hex(value, width)\n  *_guid           Guid(kind, raw): kind \"text\" = the stored string VERBATIM (D13 MSI \"{DD1A...}\"), \"bytes_le\" =\n                   a binary GUID as .NET Guid.ToString() = str(uuid.UUID(bytes_le=raw)) (D12 MVID, lowercase, no braces)\n  *_dimensions_pixels  (w, h) -> \"WxH\"                                  (D4/D5)\n  *_present / has_* / is_*   bool -> \"true\" / \"false\"                  (D3)\n  *_names / json kind        list -> compact JSON, separators (\",\", \":\"), non-ASCII kept   (D8)\n  *_version        (major, minor) -> \"x.y\"; a string passes through    (D6)\n  counts           int -> base-10                                      (D7)\n  enums            mapped case-insensitively onto answer_format.accepted_values when the contract lists them\nA plain str is already spelled (verbatim artifact text, or the literal \"none\" for an absent field).\n\n`alternates(aid, value)` = other plausible spellings of the same value (hex widths/case/prefix, GUID braces/case/\nbyte order, dimension separators, booleans), most plausible first, minus every GM-REJECTED spelling in lib.knowledge.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport re\nimport uuid\nfrom collections import namedtuple\n\nHex = namedtuple(\"Hex\", \"value width\")          # width = hex DIGITS of the struct field (u16 -> 4, u32 -> 8, u64 -> 16)\nGuid = namedtuple(\"Guid\", \"kind raw\")           # kind: \"text\" (stored string) | \"bytes_le\" | \"bytes_be\" (16 raw bytes)\nDims = namedtuple(\"Dims\", \"width height\")\n\n_UNN = re.compile(r\"_u(8|16|32|64)_hex$\")\n\n\ndef hex_width(field, raw=None):\n    \"\"\"Digits for a *_hex field: the uNN suffix wins, then *_rva_hex (u32), then the extractor's Hex.width.\"\"\"\n    m = _UNN.search(field or \"\")\n    if m:\n        return int(m.group(1)) // 4\n    if (field or \"\").endswith(\"_rva_hex\"):\n        return 8\n13:  *_names / json kind        list -> compact JSON, separators (\",\", \":\"), non-ASCII kept   (D8)\n16:  enums            mapped case-insensitively onto answer_format.accepted_values when the contract lists them\n49:    return [str(v) for v in vals] if isinstance(vals, (list, tuple)) else []\n63:def spell(fmt, field, raw, q=None):\n83:    if isinstance(raw, (list, dict)):\n95:    \"\"\"Every GM-REJECTED spelling recorded in lib.knowledge (`*_REJECTED` lists/tuples of strings).\"\"\"\n107:                elif isinstance(x, (list, tuple)):\nfrom xml.etree import ElementTree as ET\n\n\ndef external_relationship_targets(data, ctx=None):\n    try:\n        z = zipfile.ZipFile(io.BytesIO(data))\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 - not a package\n        return None\n    out = []\n    for n in z.namelist():\n        if not n.lower().endswith(\".rels\"):\n            continue\n        try:\n            root = ET.fromstring(z.read(n))\n        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 - a malformed part\n            continue\n        for el in root.iter():\n            if el.tag.rsplit(\"}\", 1)[-1] == \"Relationship\" and (el.get(\"TargetMode\") or \"\").lower() == \"external\":\n                out.append(el.get(\"Target\") or \"\")\n    return sorted(out)\nlib/playbook.py:221:        rule=\"`ooxml.external_relationship_targets` = every TargetMode=\\\"External\\\" Relationship Target across ALL \"\nlib/playbook.py:223:             \"Internal relationships (no TargetMode) are the decoys.\",\nlib/knowledge.py:213:# d15-ooxml-NNN-ooxml-external-relationship-targets (\"Determine ooxml.external_relationship_targets for\nlib/knowledge.py:217:# lib.meta.ooxml.external_relationship_targets.\nlib/knowledge.py:334:# NOT more probing. Both batch-launcher-control and batch-relay-control take this one (identical `if defined` construct).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5884df0f-5763-41eb-8262-7929a0ca7af8","uuid":"74b08fe5-a34c-427f-a249-5f17fc40411a","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:42:03.515Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Suffix-driven GM spelling for metadata-forensics fields (the naming LAWS of lib/knowledge.py, in one place).\n\nAn extractor returns a TYPED raw value; `spell(fmt, field, raw, q)` renders it the way the GM confirmed for that kind of\nfield, keyed on the field name's SUFFIX (never on the day):\n\n  *_uNN_hex        0x + lowercase hex zero-padded to NN/4 digits        (D9  pe.coff_machine_u16_hex \"0x014c\")\n  *_rva_hex        0x + 8 digits (u32 struct width)                    (D10 \"0x00065bd0\"; \"0x65bd0\" REJECTED)\n  *_hex            0x + the struct width the extractor gives via Hex(value, width)\n  *_guid           Guid(kind, raw): kind \"text\" = the stored string VERBATIM (D13 MSI \"{DD1A...}\"), \"bytes_le\" =\n                   a binary GUID as .NET Guid.ToString() = str(uuid.UUID(bytes_le=raw)) (D12 MVID, lowercase, no braces)\n  *_dimensions_pixels  (w, h) -> \"WxH\"                                  (D4/D5)\n  *_present / has_* / is_*   bool -> \"true\" / \"false\"                  (D3)\n  *_names / json kind        list -> compact JSON, separators (\",\", \":\"), non-ASCII kept   (D8)\n  *_version        (major, minor) -> \"x.y\"; a string passes through    (D6)\n  counts           int -> base-10                                      (D7)\n  enums            mapped case-insensitively onto answer_form