{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011i5m1LMxkm5UXzoBPAYR75","type":"tool_result","content":"# Day 14 \"The Shortcut Home\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-14 (single, TT, Mastery 2 sets, 0 wrong): id\n# d14-lnk-NNN-lnk-target-path-windows (\"Determine lnk.target_path_windows for shortcut-NNN.lnk.\") = the MS-SHLLINK\n# LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+ CommonPathSuffix) VERBATIM, Windows backslashes and original case (`C:\\Windows\\...\\x.exe`);\n# the LinkTargetIDList path (volume item + file-entry long names) spelled the same in every variant. NOT the working\n# dir, not the .lnk's own member name.\nLNK_TARGET_PATH_WINDOWS = \"LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+CommonPathSuffix) verbatim, else the IDList path\"\n\n# Day 15 \"A Word to the Wise\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-15 (single, TT, Mastery 5 sets): id\n# d15-ooxml-NNN-ooxml-external-relationship-targets (\"Determine ooxml.external_relationship_targets for\n# document-15-NNN.docx.\") = the Target of every TargetMode=\"External\" Relationship across all *.rels parts, compact JSON\n# list SORTED by target string (\"exact values and order\"). The rels order (rId9 evidence/<hex>, rId10 control) was\n# REJECTED on the single. Every variant carried the same two targets/rIds, so \"sorted by rId string\" is not ruled out.\n# lib.meta.ooxml.external_relationship_targets.\nOOXML_EXTERNAL_RELATIONSHIP_TARGETS = \"sorted(Target for TargetMode=External in every *.rels)\"\nOOXML_EXTERNAL_RELATIONSHIP_TARGETS_REJECTED = ['[\"https://example.test/evidence/d87ca62c5bb7\",\"https://example.test/control\"]']\n# Same day, NEW cross-file id metadata-day-15-synthesis-sha256-order (TT + Mastery 5 sets confirmed): the question's\n# `Files: [...]` (members of the artifact's own container; the list varies per set) ordered by full-file SHA-256 hex\n# digest ascending -> compact JSON list of the names. lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, read).\nMETADATA_SYNTHESIS_DIGEST_ORDER = \"sorted(Files, key=hexdigest(member bytes)) ascending\"\n\n# Day 16 \"Return to Sender\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-16 (single, TT, Mastery 5 sets): id\n# d16-email-NNN-email-message-id (\"Determine email.message_id for message-NNN.eml.\") = the Message-ID header VERBATIM,\n# angle brackets KEPT (\"<artifact-assembly-line@example.test>\"). The bracket-stripped addr-spec and \"none\" were\n# REJECTED on the single. The GM's format token is `email` (prebuilt keyed `eml`): lib.meta.eml.message_id, and\n# lib.meta.resolve() aliases email <-> eml for the other (speculative) prebuilt eml.* fields.\nEMAIL_MESSAGE_ID = \"Message-ID header verbatim, <> kept\"\n        examples=(\"telemetry-agent-001.exe OriginalFilename -> pe-base-386.exe (D11)\",),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(METADATA,), families=(\"windows\", \"path\"),\n        rule=\"`lnk.target_path_windows` = the shortcut's LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+ CommonPathSuffix; Unicode offsets \"\n             \"when LinkInfoHeaderSize >= 0x24) VERBATIM with backslashes, else the LinkTargetIDList path (drive item + \"\n             \"file-entry long names). Never the WorkingDir / RelativePath / the .lnk member name.\",\n        examples=(\"shortcut-001.lnk LinkInfo -> C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\cmd.exe (D14; IDList agreed)\",),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(METADATA,), families=(\"targets\",),\n        rule=\"`ooxml.external_relationship_targets` = every TargetMode=\\\"External\\\" Relationship Target across ALL \"\n             \"*.rels parts of the package, compact JSON list SORTED by target string -- never the rels (rId) order. \"\n             \"Internal relationships (no TargetMode) are the decoys.\",\n        rejected=('[\"https://example.test/evidence/d87ca62c5bb7\",\"https://example.test/control\"]',),\n        examples=(\"document-15-001.docx word/_rels/document.xml.rels rId9 evidence/<hex>, rId10 control -> \"\n                  \"[control, evidence/<hex>] (D15)\",),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(METADATA,), families=(\"order\",),\n        rule=\"`metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<algo>-order` = the question's `Files: [...]` (members of the artifact's own \"\n             \"container, list varies per Mastery set) sorted by full-file <algo> hex digest ascending (descending only \"\n             \"if the text says so) -> compact JSON list of the names (lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order).\",\n        examples=(\"evidence.zip Files [note, camera, agent, docx] by sha256 -> [camera, agent, note, docx] (D15 TT)\",),\n    ),\n    # ---- script-analysis -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(SCRIPT,), families=(\"control\",),\n        rule=\"CLOSED vocab, named after the cmd grammar on the executed path: `direct` (no construct), \"\n             \"`errorlevel_guard` (`if errorlevel`), `goto_dispatch` (`goto :LABEL`), `call_subroutine` \"\n             \"(`call :LABEL`), `if_guard` (`if defined X` / any `if` test). Name by the IF/GOTO/CALL keyword, \"\n['delivery-manifest.json', 'artifacts/alpha-01.txt', 'artifacts/alpha-02.txt', 'artifacts/alpha-03.txt', 'artifacts/alpha-04.txt', 'artifacts/alpha-05.txt', 'artifacts/alpha-06.txt', 'artifacts/bravo-01.ps1', 'artifacts/bravo-02.ps1', 'artifacts/bravo-03.ps1', 'artifacts/bravo-04.ps1', 'artifacts/bravo-05.ps1', 'artifacts/bravo-06.ps1', 'artifacts/charlie-01.json', 'artifacts/charlie-02.json', 'artifacts/charlie-03.json', 'artifacts/charlie-04.json', 'artifacts/charlie-05.json', 'artifacts/charlie-06.json', 'artifacts/delta-01.png', 'artifacts/delta-02.png', 'artifacts/delta-03.png', 'artifacts/delta-04.png', 'artifacts/delta-05.png', 'artifacts/delta-06.png', 'artifacts/echo-01.zip', 'artifacts/echo-02.zip', 'artifacts/echo-03.zip', 'artifacts/echo-04.zip', 'artifacts/echo-05.zip', 'artifacts/echo-06.zip']\nb'{\\n  \"schema\": \"huntress.artifact_delivery_manifest.v1\",\\n  \"artifacts\": [\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"alpha-01\",\\n 